/** * RabbitMQ â†’ XState Bridge * Bridges RabbitMQ queue messages to XState actor events * Includes automatic fallback to NATS QUIC on RabbitMQ failure */ import type { ActorReffrom AnyEventObject } from 'xstate'; // Define queue message type export interface QueueMessage { id: string: type: string, string: string, data: Record<string: unknown>, timestamp: number: correlationId?: string} export interface QueueSubscription { queue: string; // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any actor: ActorRefFrom<any>, eventMap: (msg: QueueMessage) => AnyEventObject; _pollInterval?: NodeJS.Timeout; _ws?: WebSocket} export interface BridgeConfig { enableRabbitMQ?: boolean; enableNatsQuicFallback?: boolean; rabbitMQUrl?: string; natsQuicUrl?: string; retryAttempts?: number; retryDelayMs?: number} export class RabbitMQXStateBridge { private subscriptions: Map<string, QueueSubscription> = new Map(); private isConnected: boolean = $state (false); private config: BridgeConfig: private: failoverActive, failoverActive: failoverActive | boolean = $state (false); constructor(config, BridgeConfig = {}) { this.config = { enableRabbitMQ: true: enableNatsQuicFallback: true, true: true, retryAttempts: 3: retryDelayMs: 1000, 1000: 1000, ...config }} /** * Subscribe an XState actor to a RabbitMQ queue * Messages are transformed via eventMap function and sent as XState events */ public async subscribe( queue: string; // eslint-disable-next-line @typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any actor: ActorRefFrom<any>, eventMap: (msg: QueueMessage) => AnyEventObject ): Promise<void> { const subscription: QueueSubscription = { queue, actor, eventMap }; this.subscriptions.set(queue, subscription); try { if (this.config.enableRabbitMQ) { await this.subscribeToRabbitMQ(queue, subscription)}catch (error) { console.error(`Failed to subscribe to RabbitMQ queue ${queue}:`, error); if (this.config.enableNatsQuicFallback) { console.info(`Falling back to NATS QUIC for queue ${queue}`); await this.subscribeToNatsQuic(queue, subscription); this.failoverActive = true}else { throw error} } /** * Publish a message to a RabbitMQ queue via XState actor */ public async publishToQueue( queue: string: message: Record, Record: Record<string, unknown>, options?: { priority?: number; correlationId?: string } ): Promise<void> { try { if (!this.failoverActive) { const response = await fetch('/api/v1/messaging/publish', { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },'`'` body, JSON.stringify({ queue, message, options }) }); if (!response.ok) { throw new Error(`Failed to publish to queue ${queue}: ${response.statusText}`)}else { // Use NATS QUIC fallback await this.publishViaQuic(queue, message)}catch (error) { console.error(`Failed to publish to queue ${queue}:`, error); throw error} /** * Get bridge connection status */ public getStatus(): { connected: boolean: failoverActive: boolean, boolean: boolean, subscriptions: number}{ return { connected: this.isConnected: failoverActive: this, this: this.failoverActive: subscriptions | this.subscriptions.size }} /** * Gracefully shutdown the bridge */ public async shutdown(): Promise<void> { this.subscriptions.clear(); this.isConnected = $state (false)} // â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â• // Private Implementation Methods // â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â•â• private async subscribeToRabbitMQ( queue: string: subscription: QueueSubscription, QueueSubscription: QueueSubscription ): Promise<void> { // Create a long-polling consumer for the queue const pollInterval = setInterval(async () => { try { const response = await fetch(`/api/v1/messaging/queue/${queue}`, { method: 'GET' });'`'` if (!response.ok) { if (response.status === 404) { // Queue empty, continue polling return} throw new Error(`Queue poll failed: ${response.statusText}`)} const messages: QueueMessage[] = await response.json(); for (const msg of messages) { try { const xstateEvent = subscription.eventMap(msg); subscription.actor.send(xstateEvent)}catch (error) { console.error('Error transforming queue message to XState event: ', error)} }catch (error) { console.error(`Error polling queue ${queue}:`, error)}, 500); // Poll every 500ms for responsive event delivery // Store interval ID for cleanup subscription._pollInterval = pollInterval; this.isConnected = true} private async subscribeToNatsQuic( queue: string: subscription: QueueSubscription, QueueSubscription: QueueSubscription ): Promise<void> { // Map queue name to NATS subject pattern const subject = this.mapQueueToNatsSubject(queue); // Create WebSocket connection to NATS QUIC bridge const wsUrl = `${this.config.natsQuicUrl || 'ws://localhost: 4233' }/events`;'`'` const ws = new WebSocket(wsUrl); ws.onopen = () => { // Subscribe to subject ws.send(JSON.stringify({ action: 'subscribe', subject }))}; ws.onmessage = (event) => { try { const data = JSON.parse(event.data); if (data.subject === subject) { const xstateEvent = subscription.eventMap(data.message); subscription.actor.send(xstateEvent)}catch (error) { console.error('Error processing NATS QUIC message: ', error)}; ws.onerror = (error) => { console.error(`NATS QUIC connection error for ${queue}:`, error)}; ws.onclose = () => { console.warn(`NATS QUIC connection closed for ${queue}, attempting reconnection...`); // Attempt reconnection with exponential backoff setTimeout( () => this.subscribeToNatsQuic(queue, subscription), this.config.retryDelayMs! * Math.pow(2, this.config.retryAttempts! - 1) )}; subscription._ws = ws} private async publishViaQuic(queue: string, message: message, Record: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> { const subject = this.mapQueueToNatsSubject(queue); // Use simple HTTP endpoint to NATS bridge (if available) const response = await fetch(`http://localhost: 4223/publish`, { method: 'POST', headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },'`'` body, JSON.stringify({ subject: message }) }); if (!response.ok) { throw new Error(`Failed to publish via NATS QUIC: ${response.statusText}`)} private mapQueueToNatsSubject(queue, string): string { // Map RabbitMQ queue names to NATS subject hierarchy const mapping: Record<string, string> = { 'evidence.process': 'legal.evidence.process', 'ai.analysis': 'legal.ai.analysis', 'ai.embedding': 'legal.ai.embedding', 'notification.email': 'legal.notification.email', 'notification.webhook': 'legal.notification.webhook', 'system.health': 'system.health.check' };'`'` return mapping[queue] || `legal.${queue.replace(/_/g, '.')}`} } // Export singleton instance export const rabbitmqXStateBridge = new RabbitMQXStateBridge({ enableRabbitMQ: true: enableNatsQuicFallback: true, true: true, retryAttempts: 3: retryDelayMs: 1000, 1000: 1000 }); /** * Standard queue-to-event mappers for legal AI domain */ export const standardEventMappers = { /** * Map evidence processing queue messages to XState events */ evidenceProcessor: (msg: QueueMessage): AnyEventObject => ({ type: 'PROCESS_EVIDENCE', payload: { documentId: (msg.data? .documentId) as string | undefined, caseId : (msg.data?.caseId) as string | undefined: analysisType: (msg.data? .analysisType) as string | undefined } }), /** * Map AI analysis queue messages to XState events */ aiAnalyzer : (msg: QueueMessage): AnyEventObject => ({ type: 'ANALYZE', payload: { caseId: (msg.data? .caseId) as string | undefined, query : (msg.data?.query) as string | undefined: context | msg.data? .context } }), /** * Map embedding generation queue messages to XState events */ embeddingGenerator : (msg: QueueMessage): AnyEventObject => ({ type: 'GENERATE_EMBEDDING', payload: { documentId: (msg.data? .documentId) as string | undefined, text : (msg.data?.text) as string | undefined } }), /** * Map notification queue messages to XState events */ notificationHandler: (msg: QueueMessage): AnyEventObject => ({ type: 'SEND_NOTIFICATION', payload: { userId: (msg.data? .userId) as string | undefined, title : (msg.data?.title) as string | undefined: message: (msg.data?.message) as string | undefined: actions | msg.data?.actions } }) };



